{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "קרב אל המזבח", :translit "krav el ha-mizbe'ach", :gloss "Draw near to the altar"} {:he "ב' תגין על רי\"ש", :translit "be't tagin al reish", :gloss "two tags on the resh"} {:he "קרני השור", :translit "karnei ha-shor", :gloss "horns of the ox"} {:he "חטא העגל", :translit "chet ha-'egel", :gloss "sin of the calf"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Two tagin (decorative crowns) on the resh of 'קרב' signal Aaron's hesitation"} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic wordplay: the altar appeared as horns of an ox because of the golden calf"}], :frame {:text "Aaron was ashamed to approach the altar because of his role in the golden calf, and the altar appeared to him in the form of a golden calf. Moses urged him to draw near, saying: you have been chosen. The link between Aaron's shame and the calf is elaborated at Leviticus Rabbah 13:6 and Tanhuma Acharei Mot 6. The broader midrashic tradition that crowns on letters carry meaning is attested in Menachot 29b.", :sources ["Leviticus Rabbah 13:6" "Tanhuma Acharei Mot 6" "Menachot 29b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וכפר", :translit "ve-chiper", :gloss "and atone"} {:he "וכפר על העם", :translit "ve-chiper al ha-'am", :gloss "and atone upon the people"} {:he "וכפר על חטאתינו", :translit "ve-chiper al chatoteinu", :gloss "and atone upon our sin"} {:he "קטרת", :translit "ketoret", :gloss "incense"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וכפר" "וכפר על העם" "וכפר על חטאתינו"]}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that the incense offering atones, deriving from the episode where Aaron took incense and stood between the living and the dead to halt the plague (Numbers 17:11–13), and further connects atonement through incense to Numbers 17:12. The rhetorical analogy the Ba'al HaTurim draws — 'just as a sacrifice atones, so too incense' — follows the hermeneutic principle of comparison used in Yoma 43a.", :sources ["Numbers 17:12" "Yoma 43a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Two tagin (decorative crowns) on the resh of 'קרב' signal Aaron's hesitation", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic wordplay: the altar appeared as horns of an ox because of the golden calf", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וכפר" "וכפר על העם" "וכפר על חטאתינו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וכפר", :refs ["Exodus 30:10" "Leviticus 4:20" "Leviticus 4:26" "Leviticus 4:31" "Leviticus 4:35" "Leviticus 5:6" "Leviticus 5:10" "Leviticus 5:13"], :n 38, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וכפר על העם", :refs ["Numbers 17:12"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "וכפר על חטאתינו", :refs ["Psalms 79:9"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:51.856743387Z", :model "glm-5.2"}